-- title:
--   Tₚ is congruent mod p to Hecke operators away from p
-- statement:
--   Let $N$ be a nonzero natural number and assume that the weight-two cusp forms for $\Gamma_0(N)$ have an integral structure in the sense of [`CuspForm.HasIntegralStructure`](def/CuspForm_IntegralStructure.html#L6), i.e. the $\mathbb{C}$-span of the $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule [`CuspForm.intLattice N 2`](def/CuspForm_IntegralStructure.html#L3) — the $\mathbb{Z}$-span of those cusp forms all of whose $q$-expansion coefficients are rational integers — is the whole space $S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$. Let $p$ be a prime with $p \ne 2$ and $p \nmid N$. For a set $S \subseteq \mathbb{N}$, [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) denotes the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb{C}}(S_2(\Gamma_0(N)))$ generated by the operators `heckeTLin` attached to the primes $\ell \nmid N$ with $\ell \notin S$ together with the operators `heckeULin` attached to the primes $q \mid N$ with $q \notin S$. The assertion is that there exist $t'$ in [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 {p}`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18), the subalgebra generated by the $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell \nmid N$ with $\ell \ne p$ and all the $U_q$ for primes $q \mid N$, and $t''$ in [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 ∅`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18), the full weight-two Hecke algebra of level $N$, such that the endomorphism `heckeTLin 2 hp hpN` of $S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$, i.e. the operator $T_p$ given by $f \mapsto U_p f + f \mid_2 \mathrm{diag}$-matrix at $p$, equals $t' + p \cdot t''$.
--
--   This is the congruence $T_p \equiv t' \pmod p$ underlying Ribet's lemma on generation of the Hecke algebra by operators of index prime to $p$, the second claim in Wiles's treatment; classically it rests on duality between the Hecke algebra and $q$-expansions together with Katz's theorem on the theta operator in characteristic $p$. It is used by [`CuspForm.exists_not_dvd_and_smul_mem_heckeAlgebra_of_finite`](thm.html#CuspForm.exists_not_dvd_and_smul_mem_heckeAlgebra_of_finite) to show that the subalgebra generated by the Hecke operators outside a finite set of primes has index prime to $p$ in the full Hecke algebra.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CuspForm_exists_mem_heckeAlgebra_singleton_heckeTLin_eq_add_smul_of_ne_two.lean

import Definitions.Def_CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra
import Definitions.Def_CuspForm_IntegralStructure

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

set_option autoImplicit false

theorem CuspForm.exists_mem_heckeAlgebra_singleton_heckeTLin_eq_add_smul_of_ne_two
    (N : ℕ) [NeZero N] (hint : CuspForm.HasIntegralStructure N 2)
    (p : ℕ) (hp : p.Prime) (hp2 : p ≠ 2) (hpN : ¬ p ∣ N) :
    ∃ t' ∈ CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 ({p} : Set ℕ),
      ∃ t'' ∈ CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 (∅ : Set ℕ),
        (CuspForm.heckeTLin 2 hp hpN :
            Module.End ℂ (CuspForm (CongruenceSubgroup.Gamma0 N) 2)) = t' + (p : ℤ) • t'' := by sorry
